---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const description = "StocksWatch privacy and sponsorship disclosure: current local preferences, external links, future email plans, and labeled advertising controls.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy & sponsorship"
  description={description}
  allowAds={false}
  activeNav="nbis"
  canonicalPath="/privacy.html"
>
  <article class="policy-page container">
    <p class="nbis-eyebrow">StocksWatch / Transparency</p>
    <h1>Privacy &amp; sponsorship</h1>
    <p class="policy-lede">A plain-language description of how this static research desk is designed today and what changes before email or advertising is enabled.</p>

    <section>
      <h2>Current site behavior</h2>
      <p>StocksWatch is a static, source-linked research site. It does not currently provide accounts, payments, or an email subscription. The theme choice and the optional “Follow this desk” preference are stored locally in your browser so the interface can remember your choice. They are not sent to StocksWatch.</p>
      <p>The site links to company, SEC, and provider pages. Those destinations have their own privacy practices and are outside StocksWatch control.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Future email brief</h2>
      <p>The planned “NBIS Close” email brief is not active yet. Before collecting an address, StocksWatch will select an email provider, publish consent and unsubscribe details, and add the provider’s data-processing terms to this page.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Advertising and sponsorship</h2>
      <p>Advertising is supplemental to the research product. Any future ad units will be manual, clearly labeled “Sponsored,” placed after substantial research content, and disabled unless the domain, publisher account, unit IDs, and review requirements are satisfied. Sponsor relationships will not control editorial conclusions.</p>
      <p>Third-party advertising may use cookies or similar technologies when enabled. No live ad units are required for the site to operate.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Data quality and financial framing</h2>
      <p>Market and company data can be delayed, incomplete, restated, or wrong. Verify material claims against the latest company filing. Automated readouts and scenario assumptions are educational context, not investment advice or guaranteed outcomes.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="policy-callout">This is a product disclosure, not legal advice. Review it for the jurisdictions and providers involved before enabling email collection, analytics, or advertising.</div>
    <p><a href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL}>← Return to StocksWatch</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy-page { max-width: 820px; padding: clamp(4.5rem, 10vw, 8rem) 0 5rem; }
  .policy-page h1 { margin: .7rem 0 1rem; color: var(--text); font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 7vw, 5.8rem); letter-spacing: -.08em; line-height: .95; }
  .policy-lede { max-width: 48rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .policy-page section { padding-top: 2.8rem; }
  .policy-page h2 { margin: 0 0 .65rem; color: var(--text); font-size: 1.65rem; letter-spacing: -.05em; }
  .policy-page p { color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .policy-page a { color: var(--accent); }
  .policy-callout { margin: 2.8rem 0 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: .75rem; background: var(--surface); color: var(--muted); font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.6; }
</style>
